	// ClickToReceive: Click to Receive
	// ClickToContinue: Click to Continue
	// ClickOrWaitToContinue: Click/Wait to Continue
}

FirstMetSupCal: {
	// Rolename1: ???
	// Rolename2: Brimstone Witch
	// Rolename3: Halibut
	// Line1: I hadn't expected you to kill my 'sister' so soon.
	// Line2: You are growing... faster than anticipated.
	// Line3: I recognize you... You're...
	// Line4: The Brimstone Witch?! The one who incinerated half the ocean?!
	// Line5: Hah?! Heh... To think someone... or some*fish*... actually recognizes me. You are amusing, I'll give you that.
	// Line6: ...But why are you alive? I distinctly remember the Brimstone Witch died... last century.
	// Line7: An interesting fish, indeed. My consciousness was forged into the brimstone flame long ago. This body... it is merely a corpse, puppeteered by the flames.
	// Line8: ...A living mind in an inhuman vessel, bound to the world by a medium... You've become... an aberration?!
	// Line9: Your comprehension is too limited. You could not possibly understand my state of being.
	// Line10: Besides, that is not why I am here...
	// QuestionLine: Well... what is your choice?
	// Choice1Text: (Draw weapon)
	// Choice2Text: (Remain silent)
	// Choice1Response: Then let me measure your worth.
	// Choice2Response: ...Pathetic. A 'small fry', indeed. Very well, take this as a greeting gift. We will meet again.
	// NoFishLine1: You killed my 'sister' far sooner than I expected. And you came alone?
	// NoFishLine2: You are growing stronger than I anticipated.
	// NoFishLine3: You ask why I am still alive? It seems you have begun to touch upon truths you were not meant to know.
	// NoFishLine4: My consciousness was forged into the brimstone flame long ago. This body... it is merely a corpse, puppetes
	// NoFishLine5: But it is pointless. Your comprehension is too limited to grasp my state of being.
	// NoFishLine6: Of course, I did not reveal myself merely to explain these trivialities.
}

