}

SupCalDisplayText: {
	// SummonWithProverbs: You... you actually came wearing that ring... Very well. I will show no mercy.
	// SummonWithoutProverbs: Hahaha... This moment... I have awaited it for so long.
	// SummonRematchWithProverbs: You're still wearing that ring...
	// SummonRematchWithoutProverbs: You again... It seems your understanding of death is still... insufficient.
	// StartLowHealth: You already look to be on your last breath.
	// StartMediumHealth: Your technique still requires improvement.
	// StartDefault: How strange. You should be dead already...
	// StartRematchLowHealth: You already look to be on your last breath.
	// StartRematchMediumHealth: Wounded? How interesting.
	// StartRematchDefault: How strange. You should be dead already...
	// BH3WithHalibut: Wielding such... aberrant... power in a mortal vessel... To have come this far, you are indeed worthy of respect.
	// BH3WithoutHalibut: You are skilled... but when will you realize you are merely attacking a plume of fire in vain?
	// BrothersWithHalibut: It is time you met my family. They failed on the path to becoming... 'other'. Do not follow their example.
	// BrothersWithoutHalibut: It is time you met my family. Should you die at another's hand, I will keep your soul here.
	// Phase2WithHalibut: Are you certain you do not wish to beg for mercy?
	// Phase2WithoutHalibut: Are you certain you do not wish to beg?
	// BH4Text: Stand still and face me!
	// SeekerRingText: Your power comes from external sources. As you are, you are nothing... It reminds me of that hypocrite.
	// BH5Text: The scales of victory are... uncertain. You only need to stand still for a moment to change this, understood?
	// Sepulcher2Text: If only one of us can live today... who do you think I *want* it to be?
	// Desperation1Text: JUST... STAND... STILL... YOU... SMALL FRY!
	// Desperation2Text: Don't get arrogant—I was merely toying with you before!
	// Desperation3Text: *cough*... *cough*... I admit, I am not in peak condition today.
	// Desperation4Text: It seems... I have lost. Meeting you... has truly been a blessing.
	// Acceptance1Text: This... is the happiest I have been in a hundred years...
	// Acceptance2Text: Perhaps... you truly can end this damned era.
	/* Story1:
		'''
		The wood of this crossbow is hewn from a pitch-black coffin buried for a century. 
		It reeks of an earthy stench that simply won't wash off.
		Down there, it served to suppress a horror that even I found difficult to handle.
		Against such things, pure destruction is meaningless. They cannot be killed.
		Fire the wedge. Pin them back to the earth and force them into silence.
		As for why you throw the crossbow first?
		Hah... If the guest isn't tainted by the scent of the casket, how will the coffin know who to collect?
		''' */
	/* Story2:
		'''
		This wretched blade is dull because it doesn't cut flesh—it severs mediums.
		When I was still an apprentice, a mouth that would never close grew upon my teacher's heart.
		He died later, yet that heart kept beating. With every beat, the mouth screamed, 
		and one person around us simply vanished.
		To survive, I had to gouge that heart out before its next beat.
		Even now, it hungers to hear the sound of a heart being carved out again.
		''' */
	/* Story3:
		'''
		Find it heavy? Good. It should be.
		It is laced with excessive gold and wreathed in Brimstone flames, 
		all to lock down the six restless ghostly hands upon the blade.
		Those three idiots tried to dismember and stitch themselves together to delay their own 'recovery'... 
		but they ended up as a twisted monstrosity that knows only how to strangle.
		Grip it tight. Once the Brimstone suppression fails, the first neck they will snap is yours.
		Snapping the neck of whoever touches the blade... that is the only instinct they have left.
		''' */
	/* Story4:
		'''
		Mortals call this magic, but I call it... borrowing.
		This is no spellbook; it is a high-density cage.
		Every page seals a horror that once silenced entire city-states into death.
		''' */
}

SupCalDisplayTextByBossRush: {
	// SummonBossRush: Heh… The aura on you almost reminds me of the one who has long since perished.
	// SummonBossRushWithProverbs: That ring… even a mere remnant like me can feel its trembling.
	// StartBossRush: I may be nothing more than an anomalous construct born from the Golden Soul… but there are duties even I must fulfill.
	// BH2BossRush: Your strength is impressive… yet still insufficient.
	// BH3BossRush: The shadows of the past… long since reduced to ashes, scattered on the path you walk. Heh…
	// BrothersBossRush: These souls… shadows of shadows. The more you copy something, the sadder it becomes, don’t you think?
	// Phase2BossRush: Even a fabricated life can have something worth fighting for.
	// BH4BossRush: Stand still! Let me see if you can truly bear the weight of an era!
	// SeekerRingBossRush: Your power resembles that person in her memories far too closely… mere coincidence?
	// BH5BossRush: As an anomalous creation, my purpose is to face this very moment.
	// Sepulcher2BossRush: The final trial begins now… show me whether you are worthy of carrying her path forward.
	// Desperation1BossRush: Even a fragment…
	// Desperation2BossRush: Don’t assume victory is yours just yet…
	// Desperation3BossRush: Heh… the life of a shadow was fragile from the start…
	// Desperation4BossRush: You’ve won… but her journey is far from over.
	// Acceptance1BossRush: Perhaps… this is where I was always meant to end.
	// Acceptance2BossRush: Good luck… small fry.
}

SupCalDisplayTextNormal: {
	// SummonText: This sea of brimstone fire... even a vengeful spirit would feel the scorch, wouldn't they?
	// SummonRematchText: Prove it to me. Survive.
	// StartText: Mortal shells are always so fragile in this heat... or perhaps, you can surprise me?
	// StartRematchText: Not burnt to cinders yet? Then let us begin again, until you are forged into steel... or reduced to ash.
	// BH2Text: You have not yet collapsed within the flames... you burn slower than I imagined.
	// BH2RematchText: I admit you possess some courage, but your skill is still far from sufficient.
	// BH3Text: You traveled all this way, just to subject that mortal frame to pain?
	// BH3RematchText: The last time I rained down such calamity was a century ago. Do you wish to experience it as well?
	// BrothersText: They once burned everything for the sake of that path... Now, let these ashes measure your worth.
	// BrothersRematchText: Perhaps they are merely empty shells with a sliver of soul, but they are more than enough to deal with you.
	// Phase2Text: From here on... the flames will no longer be restrained. Do not die too quickly.
	// Phase2RematchText: Once again, let us begin.
	// BH4Text: Do not think you can escape my grasp!
	// BH4RematchText: I am curious... did you learn anything from our first encounter?
	// SeekerRingText: How did you dodge that? This is not how it should go... Stop!
	// SeekerRingRematchText: At least my judgment was not mistaken...
	// BH5Text: I admit the battle thus far was mere child's play. Now, I will give it my all!
	// BH5RematchText: ...Isn't this exciting?
	// Sepulcher2Text: If only one of us can survive this... who do you think I *wish* it to be?
	// Sepulcher2RematchText: Pay attention. The crawling tomb approaches... and it hungers for a new tenant.
	// Desperation1Text: Just STOP!
	// Desperation2Text: If I fail here, then what was the point of it all?!
	// Desperation3Text: Someone has already walked your path to its end. It is a dead end... What makes you think *you* can be different?!
	// Desperation4Text: If you merely repeat his madness, you will be nothing more than fresh ash among these embers!
	// Acceptance1Text: I burned myself into this inhuman form, solely to find that one glimmer of hope...
	// Acceptance2Text: I have no strength left to stand...
	// Acceptance3Text: An aberration like you... perhaps you truly can carve out... a future even I have never seen.
	// Desperation1RematchText: An impressive performance. You fought well.
	// Desperation2RematchText: Without a doubt, your strength grows with every passing moment.
	// Desperation3RematchText: I truly hope you will not repeat our mistakes.
	// Desperation4RematchText: If you can forge a new path... then there is still hope for everything.
}

FirstMetTzeentch: {
	// L1: Hush... don't look back.
	// L2: I've been watching you build these little contraptions.
	// L3: Ten quantum nodes. Ten pathways. Ten possible futures.
	// L4: A cute little network. Do you have any idea how many... *things*... it will attract?
	// L5: Ah, right. I should introduce myself.
	// L6: Some call me the Oracle. Others, the Feather of Fate...
	// L7: But I'm more interested in what... *you*... would call me, right now.
	// L8: Go on. Let me hear it.
	// Choice1Text: A... Magician...?
	// Choice2Text: A Liar.
	// Choice3Text: No. I don't know you.
	// Choice1_R1: Hah! Such a... gentle term.
	// Choice1_R2: A pity. I don't perform magic. I only change facts.
	// Choice1_R3: Continue on. We'll put 'Magician' on the tab for now.
	// Choice2_R1: Ah. Direct, blunt, honest. Such precious qualities.
	// Choice2_R2: But I'm afraid I never lie.
	// Choice2_R3: I simply tell you... what is about to happen.
	// Choice2_R4: Whether you believe it or not... it has already occurred.
	// Choice3_R1: You don't? Excellent.
	// Choice3_R2: All stories begin with those words.
	// Choice3_R3: It's just... most of the endings are not very pleasant.
	// EndLine1: Well, then. We will meet again.
	// EndLine2: Soon.
}

